[h1]Dead Weight[/h1]
[i]Step on the scale. Face the truth.[/i]

[img]{{GIF_URL}}[/img]

The clinic's scale still works. Stand on it and it tells you exactly what the apocalypse did to you, to one decimal. Not kindly.

[h2]How it works[/h2]
Walk onto the beam scale's plate. The beam head reads your weight (about 2.5 seconds to settle, like the real thing). Walk off and the number goes with you. No item, no menu, nothing to craft.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]A brass and cream beam head readout, poise sliding toward your weight and settling instead of snapping, because a real scale wobbles.
[*]One decimal of precision.
[*]Left click the readout to switch between kg and lb.
[*]Right click it to switch between the beam head look and a plain native panel.
[*]Your unit and style choices are remembered between sessions.
[*]The character screen's Info tab now shows only your weight category in words (Emaciated to Obese) with its trend arrow. The exact number stays on the scale.
[*]Your survivor turns once to face the scale's column on stopping, because reading a number sideways is undignified.
[*]Two short sounds: stepping on, stepping off.
[*]A "Step on Scale" option at the top of the scale's right click menu, with its own small hand icon, walks you there.
[*]Every local splitscreen player gets their own readout.
[*]The scale reads everyone on it, survivors, animals and zombies, added up. Stand one square away and you read them too, like a doctor weighing a patient.
[*]No per frame scanning: the reading only exists while someone is on the scale and you are next to it.
[*]28 languages, every one the game ships.
[/list]

[h2]Weigh others, and anything else[/h2]
Whatever stands on the scale is weighed, and anyone on it or one square away in the same room reads the same number. Two survivors together read their true combined weight: the beam rests at its end and the number stays honest. A light animal reads under 35 kg, a heavy pair over 130 kg.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/deadweight-animal.gif[/img]

A zombie has no weight in the game, so each one gets a believable invented weight, the same every time you see it. Only the first person to step on or off hears the sound.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight/main/workshop/art/deadweight-zombie.gif[/img]

[h2]Options[/h2]
Left click the readout for kg or lb. Right click it for beam head or native panel. Both are remembered automatically.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Built for Build 42, keeps Build 41 support. Singleplayer and multiplayer (client side), splitscreen aware, safe to add or remove mid save. If another mod replaces the character screen, this fails safe: the scale keeps working and the Info tab simply stays as that mod or vanilla draws it.

[h2]About the old Weight Scale[/h2]
Replaces the original item based "Weight Scale" and its full nutrition stats panel, now retired. Disable the old mod first; the two should not run together.

[h2]Translations[/h2]
28 languages included. Native speaker corrections welcome in the comments.

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/Konijima/pz-dead-weight]Source code on GitHub[/url]. Bug reports and translation fixes welcome there.

